# GitHub Pages routing

Production is deployed to https://bswanson107.github.io/golden-spoon/ with base path `/golden-spoon` (`GITHUB_PAGES=true` in CI). Local dev uses an empty base.

- Import `base` from `$app/paths` for `<a href>` attributes: `href="{base}/leagues"`.
- Use `` goto(`${base}/path`) `` for programmatic navigation — bare `goto('/')` resolves to the domain root and 404s on GitHub Pages.
- For auth/route guards, use `$page.route.id` (e.g. `/login`), not `$page.url.pathname` (e.g. `/golden-spoon/login`).
- `svelte.config.js` sets `paths.base`; do not hardcode `/golden-spoon` in source — always use `{base}`.

Optional later: point `goldenspoon.xyz` at GitHub Pages or a DNS redirect to this URL. Until then, do not rely on the custom domain.
